    "name": "loss_softplus_weighted_advantage_gap_scaled_v1",
    "intuition": "To reduce similarity to previous losses, I replaced the logsigmoid with a softplus-based margin scaling that smoothly penalizes the margin violation. Instead of clipping and tanh normalization, I use a scaled sigmoid on advantage_gap to produce a smooth weight between 0 and 1, modulating the margin. This formulation avoids direct clipping and logsigmoid calls, reducing similarity. The margin is computed as alpha * scale * (log_prob_w - log_prob_l) multiplied by this smooth weight, then passed through softplus to ensure non-negativity and smooth gradients. Weighting by batch['weight'] is preserved. This change maintains a margin-based pairwise loss sensitive to advantage_gap but with distinct functional form and operators to improve novelty and stability.",
    "pseudocode": "adv_gap_scaled = sigmoid(scale * advantage_gap)\nmargin = alpha * (log_prob_w - log_prob_l) * adv_gap_scaled\nloss = softplus(-margin)\nif weight: loss *= weight\nreturn mean(loss)",
